1
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Doctor Who: The Five Doctors is a science fiction, action,
adventure film directed by Peter Moffatt.

2
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Many incarnations of the Doctors and their old companions are taken out
of time and deposited in the Death Zone on Gallifrey.

3
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:24,000
There, they must battle the Master, Daleks, Cybermen and Yeti in order to
reach the Dark Tower and discover the Tomb of Rassilon.

4
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:30,000
The Doctor (5), played by Peter Davison.

5
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,000
The Doctor (3), played by Jon Pertwee.

6
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:42,000
The Doctor (2), played by Patrick Troughton.

7
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:48,000
The Doctor (1), played by Richard Hurndall.

8
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:54,000
The Doctor (4) (archive footage), played by Tom Baker.

9
00:45:54,000 --> 00:46:00,000
The Doctor (1) (archive footage), played by William Hartnell.

10
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Fourteen actors have portrayed the Doctor in a leading role in the
British science fiction television series Doctor Who.

11
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:12,000
The series' protagonist, the Doctor is an alien
from a species called Time Lords.

12
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
The transition to each succeeding actor is explained within the narrative through the plot device of regeneration, which
allows Time Lords a change of cellular structure when they near death, changing their appearance and personality.

13
01:06:18,000 --> 01:06:24,000
The first actor to portray the Doctor was William Hartnell beginning with
An Unearthly Child (1963) through The Tenth Planet (1966).

14
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
In the final moments of the serial, the First Doctor
regenerated into Patrick Troughton's Second Doctor.

15
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The most recent incarnation, the Fifteenth Doctor, was played by Ncuti Gatwa, who took over
the role from David Tennant following the conclusion of "The Giggle" (2023).

16
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Gatwa departed the role in "The Reality War" (2025).

17
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:48,000
Outside of television many actors have played the Doctor in various BBC-licensed
spin-offs on television, stage, radio, film, audio plays, and webcasts.

18
01:31:48,000 --> 01:31:54,000
The character's ability to periodically regenerate appearance and personality has facilitated the ability of new actors to take over the
role – in official and unofficial productions – while in most cases maintaining continuity with the television series.

19
01:36:54,000 --> 01:37:00,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
